---
import BaseLayout from "../layouts/BaseLayout.astro";
import { identity } from "../lib/data";
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Definition"
  path="/definition/"
  description="The canonical definition of Constitutional Capitalism."
>
  <article class="prose">
    <h1>The Definition of Constitutional Capitalism</h1>
    <p class="status-note">Canonical working definition — final approval pending as open decision</p>

    <blockquote class="quote">{identity.canonical_definition}</blockquote>

    <h2>Central belief</h2>
    <blockquote class="quote">{identity.central_belief}</blockquote>

    <h2>In plain terms</h2>
    <p>
      Free enterprise remains the most effective engine of wealth creation. Lasting prosperity also
      requires broad opportunity, real competition, responsible ownership, and institutions that keep
      economic power accountable to the people — whether that power is public or private.
    </p>

    <h2>What the framework preserves</h2>
    <p>
      Private property, markets, entrepreneurship, lawful profit, voluntary exchange, innovation,
      investment, competition, limited government, due process, and the rule of law.
    </p>

    <h2>What the framework changes</h2>
    <p>
      It treats public-scale economic power as a constitutional concern; expands ownership pathways;
      protects competition as liberty infrastructure; and refuses to treat ordinary work as the most
      convenient place to extract public revenue while concentrated privilege arranges exits.
    </p>

    <h2>What it is not</h2>
    <p>
      It is not abolition of private property, centralized planning, hostility to business success,
      guaranteed equality of outcome, or unchecked corporate rule. See the full boundary statement
      in the project governance documents and the comparison page.
    </p>

    <p>
      <a class="button button--solid" href="/declaration/">Read the Declaration</a>
      <a class="button button--solid" href="/compare/" style="margin-left:0.5rem;">Compare systems</a>
    </p>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>
